text.section:
Except as otherwise provided in subdivision B 2 of § 64.2-1047, a unitrust policy may provide methods for determining the amount of the net fair market value of the trust to take into account in determining the applicable value, including:

Obtaining an appraisal of an asset for which fair market value is not readily available;


Exclusion of specific assets or groups or types of assets;


Other exceptions or modifications of the treatment of specific assets or groups or types of assets;


Identification and treatment of cash or property held for distribution;


Use of:
				a. An average of fair market values over a stated number of preceding periods; or
				b. Another mathematical blend of fair market values over a stated number of preceding periods;


A limit on how much the applicable value of all assets, groups of assets, or individual assets may increase over:
				a. The corresponding applicable value for the preceding period; or
				b. A mathematical blend of applicable values over a stated number of preceding periods;


A limit on how much the applicable value of all assets, groups of assets, or individual assets may decrease below:
				a. The corresponding applicable value for the preceding period; or
				b. A mathematical blend of applicable values over a stated number of preceding periods;


The treatment of accrued income and other features of an asset that affect value; and


Determining the liabilities of the trust, including treatment of liabilities to conform with the treatment of assets under subdivisions 1 through 8.
